# Wave 2: data-common. Cross-cutting CLI for every data format a team meets
# on day one: CSV, JSON/YAML, SQLite/DuckDB, PDF, archives, metadata.
# csvkit / visidata / sqlite-utils come via `uv tool` in wave 3, not brew.
# poppler is the one heavy closure allowed here (pdftotext/pdfinfo are day-one).
# Do NOT add pdfgrep (ripgrep-all covers it). Do NOT add tesseract/ffmpeg/imagemagick
# here: those are the opt-in pdf-ocr and media layers.

brew "duckdb"
brew "sqlite"
brew "miller"
brew "yq"
brew "gron"
brew "qpdf"
brew "poppler"
brew "pandoc"
brew "ripgrep-all"
brew "sevenzip"
brew "exiftool"
